cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use feynlab in your work, please cite it as below."
title: "feynlab: a Feynman-diagram laboratory for many-body physics and Hall transport"
abstract: >-
  Companion software to Mattuck's Guide to Feynman Diagrams in the Many-Body Problem, extended
  to research-grade tools: diagram enumeration and diagrammatic Monte Carlo, perturbation
  theory, RPA/FLEX self-energies, dynamical mean-field theory with exact-diagonalisation,
  Hubbard-I and continuous-time QMC solvers (CT-HYB, CT-INT, DCA), charge self-consistent
  DFT+DMFT, lambda-corrected dynamical vertex approximation and TPSC, BCS, and anomalous,
  spin, orbital and quadrupole Hall transport (intrinsic, side jump, skew scattering) with
  Kubo-Streda ladders and Boltzmann theory. Every module is benchmarked against exact or
  published results; tutorials, quizzes and a Beamer lecture deck are included.
type: software
